{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790349523,"nonce":"zZwb7hKu7bgRVq8PD7WpJeYJJzQ=","title":"LLVM backend has no lowering for closure types, so a program holding a lambda cannot be AOT-built","message":"LLVMBackend::translate_type (crates/compiler/src/llvm_backend.rs:6417) falls through to \"Type translation not yet implemented\" for HirType::Closure. A non-capturing lambda held in a local is enough:\n\n    let double: (i64) =\u003e i64 = def(x): x * 2\n\n`zyntax compile --backend llvm` stops with \"Code generation error: Type translation not yet implemented: Closure(HirClosureType { function_type: HirFunctionType { params: [I64], returns: [I64], .. }, captures: [], call_mode: Fn })\". bench_lambda_call.zynml with the prelude import removed fails the same way, while `zynml run` prints 35000000. Under the tiered runtime a failed LLVM compile leaves the function on Cranelift, so only AOT has no fallback. NUC x86_64 and Mac arm64. The ignored case a_lambda_is_called in crates/zyntax_cli/tests/llvm_aot_zynml.rs (branch aot-reval) covers it.","files":null}]}